course: dictionary
lesson: 9030
title: Slang
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Slang is very informal words and phrases used in casual talk, like chatting with friends. Groups of people, such as young people, often create their own slang. You would not use it in formal writing, such as a school report or a letter to the head teacher.
explain: Slang changes fast and can be different from one country to another. In Liverpool, «boss» means great, but that word may not mean great anywhere else. Standard English is the everyday English you use in writing and in formal situations, and it stays the same for everyone.
explain: In the UK, slang can also be a verb. A slanging match is an angry argument where people throw insults at each other. So if someone says «we had a slanging match», they are describing a noisy fight with rude words, not a game with silly words.
fact: Slang is very informal words and phrases, used in casual talk and not in formal writing.
fact: Slang changes fast and often differs between countries and groups of people.
fact: «Boss» (Liverpool) means great, and «gutted» (Britain) means very disappointed.
fact: «Lush» (Wales) means lovely, and «mid» means average.
fact: A slanging match is an angry argument with insults.
exercise: Which of these is slang rather than standard English? | *Cool | Splendid | Magnificent | Delighted
exercise: Someone in Liverpool says «that goal was boss». What do they mean? | Angry | Tired | *Great | Hungry
exercise: Ella says, «I'm gutted that the trip was cancelled.» What does gutted mean? | Very happy | *Very disappointed | Very hungry | Very tired
test: Mia says «lush» is what people in Wales say for lovely. What does lush mean in Wales? | Lost | Loud | *Lovely | Late
test: What is a slanging match? | A friendly game of football | A dance competition | A long lesson in class | *An angry argument with insults
exam: Which sentence uses slang? | *I'm gutted about the result | The result was unfortunate | The result was extremely disappointing | I feel very sad about the result
